cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "How Fast Does a Quantum Error-Correction Decoder Need to Be? Measuring Classical Feedback Latency in Software QEC Decoders, from Simulation to IBM Device Replicas"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and figures for a study of classical feedback latency in quantum error
  correction. A look-up-table decoder for the three-qubit bit-flip code is timed in Python
  and in C, deadline violation rates at 40 microseconds are measured over six complete runs,
  and the code runs with real-time feed-forward on calibrated IBM Heron r2 and Eagle r3
  device replicas, including a sweep of logical error against decoder wait.
type: software
